 ℕ} (K : M(Y_n,Y_n)) : M(X_n,X_n) := K.submatrix (order n) (order n); its entry at i,j : X_n is K (order n i) (order n j).\nnormalizedBe (n : ℕ) : M(X_n,F_n) := (Real.sqrt 2)^(-1) • Be n.\nnormalizedBo (n : ℕ) : M(X_n,F_n) := (Real.sqrt 2)^(-1) • Bo n.\noddVector {n : ℕ} (v : F_n → ℝ) : X_n → ℝ := Sum.elim v (-v); on inl i it is v i and on inr i it is -v i.\nouter {ι : Type 0} (v : ι → ℝ) : M(ι,ι) := fun i j : ι => v i * v j. No finiteness instance is required for this definition.\n\nMAIN THEOREMS\nIn the formulas below, symbols P, S, E, Be and Bo carry the currently bound n. Write Ue = normalizedBe n, Uo = normalizedBo n, Ae = orderedBe n, Ao = orderedBo n and So = orderedS n.\ncoordinate_bridge (n : ℕ): the conjunction of (∀ i : F_n, val(order n (inl i)) = k_i AND val(order n (inr i)) = (n+n-1)-k_i); (∀ i : X_n, order n (swap i) = (order n i).rev); (∀ i : X_n, sign n i = (-1)^(val(order n i))); paired(orderedP n) = P n; and paired(orderedS n) = S n.\ninvolutions (n : ℕ): P*P = I_Xn AND E*E = I_Fn AND S*S = I_Xn AND P^T = P AND E^T = E AND S^T = S.\nbasis_relations (n : ℕ): P*Be = Be AND P*Bo = -Bo AND Be^T*Be = 2•I_Fn AND Bo^T*Bo = 2•I_Fn AND Be^T*Bo = 0 AND S*Be = Bo*E AND S*Bo = Be*E.\nsector_exchange {n : ℕ} (K : M(X_n,X_n)): KpOdd K = E*rawKe(K)*E AND KpEven K = E*rawKo(K)*E.\nordered_compressions {n : ℕ} (K : M(Y_n,Y_n)): Ae^T*K*Ae = rawKe(paired K) AND Ao^T*K*Ao = rawKo(paired K) AND Ao^T*(So*K*So)*Ao = E*(Ae^T*K*Ae)*E AND Ae^T*(So*K*So)*Ae = E*(Ao^T*K*Ao)*E.\nnormalization {n : ℕ} (K : M(X_n,X_n)): Ue^T*Ue = I_Fn AND Uo^T*Uo = I_Fn AND Ue^T*K*Ue = (1/2)•rawKe K AND Uo^T*K*Uo = (1/2)•rawKo K.\nodd_rank_one {n : ℕ} (v : F_n → ℝ): putting W = outer(oddVector v), the assertion is rawKo W = 4•outer v AND rawKe W = 0 AND KpOdd W = 0 AND (v ≠ 0 → rawKo W ≠ 0). The zero in v ≠ 0 is the zero function. Nonzero v is a premise only of the last implication.\nconvention_bridge {n : ℕ} (K : M(X_n,X_n)): (-S)*K*(-S) = Kp K AND (-S)*Be = Bo*(-E) AND (-S)*Bo = Be*(-E) AND Uo^T*(Kp K)*Uo = E*(Ue^T*K*Ue)*E AND Ue^T*(Kp K)*Ue = E*(Uo^T*K*Uo)*E.\ndistinct_sectors_counterexample: ∃ K : M(X_1,X_1), K^T = K AND P 1*K = K*P 1 AND rawKo K ≠ KpOdd K.\naudit_root: a closed conjunction, in order, of the full universally quantified propositions just displayed for coordinate_bridge, involutions, basis_relations, sector_exchange, ordered_compressions, normalization, odd_rank_one and convention_bridge, followed by the displayed existential proposition for distinct_sectors_counterexample. Each component retains its own n and K or v quantifiers. There are no additional outer parameters or hypotheses.\n\nGENERATED EQUATION THEOREMS\nBe.eq_1: ∀ (n : ℕ), Be n = Sum.elim I_Fn I_Fn.\nBo.eq_1: ∀ (n : ℕ), Bo n = Sum.elim I_Fn (-I_Fn).\nE.eq_1: ∀ (n : ℕ), E n = diagonal(fun i : F_n => (-1)^k_i).\nKp.eq_1: ∀ {n : ℕ} (K : M(X_n,X_n)), Kp K = S n*K*S n.\nP.eq_1: ∀ (n : ℕ) (i j : X_n), P n i j = if swap i = j then 1 else 0.\nS.eq_1: ∀ (n : ℕ), S n = diagonal(sign n).\nnormalizedBe.eq_1: ∀ (n : ℕ), normalizedBe n = (Real.sqrt 2)^(-1) • Be n.\nnormalizedBo.eq_1: ∀ (n : ℕ), normalizedBo n = (Real.sqrt 2)^(-1) • Bo n.\noddVector.eq_1: ∀ {n : ℕ} (v : F_n → ℝ), oddVector v = Sum.elim v (-v), an equality of functions on X_n.\norder.eq_1: ∀ (n : ℕ), order n = (Equiv.sumCongr (Equiv.refl F_n) Fin.revPerm).trans finSumFinEquiv, with both summands Fin n.\norderedBe.eq_1: ∀ (n : ℕ), orderedBe n = (Be n).submatrix (order n).symm id.\norderedBo.eq_1: ∀ (n : ℕ), orderedBo n = (Bo n).submatrix (order n).symm id.\norderedP.eq_1: ∀ (n : ℕ) (i j : Y_n), orderedP n i j = if i.rev = j then 1 else 0.\norderedS.eq_1: ∀ (n : ℕ), orderedS n = diagonal(fun i : Y_n => (-1)^k_i).\nouter.eq_1: ∀ {ι : Type 0} (v : ι → ℝ) (i j : ι), outer v i j = v i*v j.\npaired.eq_1: ∀ {n : ℕ} (K : M(Y_n,Y_n)), paired K = K.submatrix (order n) (order n).\nrawKe.eq_1: ∀ {n : ℕ} (K : M(X_n,X_n)), rawKe K = (Be n)^T*K*Be n.\nrawKo.eq_1: ∀ {n : ℕ} (K : M(X_n,X_n)), rawKo K = (Bo n)^T*K*Bo n.\nsign.eq_1: ∀ (n : ℕ), sign n = Sum.elim (fun i : F_n => (-1)^k_i) (fun i : F_n => -((-1)^k_i)), an equality of functions on X_n.\n\nGENERATED AUXILIARY THEOREMS\ncoordinate_bridge._proof_1_3: ∀ (n : ℕ) (i : F_n) (h : (n-(k_i+1))+n ≠ ((n+n)-1)-k_i), False.\ncoordinate_bridge._proof_1_4: ∀ (n : ℕ) (i : F_n) (h : (n-(k_i+1))+n ≠ (n+n)-(k_i+1)), False.\ncoordinate_bridge._proof_1_5: ∀ (n : ℕ) (i : F_n) (h : k_i ≠ (n+n)-(((n-(k_i+1))+n)+1)), False.\ncoordinate_bridge._proof_1_6: ∀ (n : ℕ) (i : F_n) (h : (((n+n)-1)-k_i)+k_i ≠ 2*(n-1)+1), False. In these four translations, h names the otherwise anonymous explicit implication premise; the conclusion is conditional on that premise.\ncoordinate_bridge._simp_1_10: for arbitrary universe levels u,v, ∀ {α : Sort u} {β : Sort v} (f : α ≃ β) {x y : α}, (f x = f y) = (x = y), where the outer equality is equality of propositions in Prop.\ninvolutions._simp_1_5: for arbitrary universe level u_1, ∀ {α : Sort u_1} {a b : α}, (a = b) = (b = a), again an equality in Prop.\nnormalization._simp_1_2: for arbitrary universe level u_1, ∀ {G : Type u_1} [inst : Semigroup G] (a b c : G), a*(b*c) = (a*b)*c.\nnormalizedBe._proof_1: the closed proposition Nat.AtLeastTwo(1+1), with no dimension parameter or other binder."
